course: dictionary
lesson: 615
title: The axle: the rod wheels turn on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An axle is a rod or bar that goes through the centre of a wheel, or joins two wheels, so the wheels can turn. Think of it as the line the wheel spins around.
explain: «A wheel and axle turns a small force on a big wheel into a stronger turn on the thin axle.» This is why the wheel and axle is a simple machine: it makes moving heavy loads easier.
explain: «Ball bearings, tiny steel balls inside a wheel's hub, let the wheel turn on its axle with very little friction.» Less friction means the wheel spins more easily.
fact: An axle is a rod or bar that a wheel turns on.
fact: Bikes, cars, trains, carts and skateboards all have axles.
fact: You may hear the phrases wheel and axle, front axle and back axle.
fact: «A water wheel at an old mill is turned by flowing water, and its axle drives gears that turn heavy millstones to grind flour.»
fact: In science lessons, you can build a model car with straws as axles.
exercise: What is an axle? | A tiny steel ball inside a hub | *A rod or bar that goes through the centre of a wheel so it can turn | A flat pad that stops a wheel from spinning | A type of tyre with air in it
exercise: In «A wheel and axle turns a small force on a big wheel into a stronger turn on the thin axle», which part is thin? | *The axle | The big wheel | The gears | The force
exercise: Which of these has an axle? | A book | A bowl of soup | A pencil case | *A skateboard
test: What do ball bearings let the wheel do with very little friction? | Turn into a bird | Stop suddenly | *Turn easily on its axle | Get heavier
test: A rod joins two wheels so they turn together. What is that rod called? | Ramp | *Axle | Pulley | Lever
exam: Why is a wheel and axle a simple machine? | It is made of gears and millstones | *It turns a small force into a stronger turn, so heavy loads are easier to move | It stops the wheel from turning | It works only when water flows over it
